{
  "_note": "Firmware capability -> SDK call. tools/gen_coverage.py reads the firmware's public headers and fails if any function here is missing, or if the firmware grows one that is not listed. That is the mechanism behind the claim 'everything the robot can do, a skill can do': it is checked, not promised.",
  "_status": {
    "exposed": "Reachable from a skill.",
    "internal": "Firmware plumbing with no meaning inside a skill (boot, the sandbox's own bookkeeping).",
    "withheld": "Deliberately not exposed. The reason is in `why` and belongs in the docs, not in someone's head."
  },
  "sources": [
    "robot/robot.h"
  ],
